{"name":"To Hell and Black","hex":"#25212a","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hell","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A place of torment where some or all sinners are believed to go after death and evil spirits are believed to be.","Synonym of underworld, an underground land of the dead without eternal punishment or with only some regions of punishment."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A place or situation of great suffering in life.","A place for gambling."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hell"},{"term":"and","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Ansus."]},{"part":"Conjunction","definitions":["As a coordinating conjunction; expressing two elements to be taken together or in addition to each other.","Yet; but."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/and"},{"term":"black","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Absorbing all light and reflecting none; dark and hueless.","Without light."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour/color perceived in the absence of light, but also when no light is reflected, but rather absorbed.","A black dye or pigment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black"}],"entries":[{"title":"To Hell and Black","blocks":[{"text":"To Hell and Black is the only studio album by American hip hop group Capital Punishment Organization. It was released through Capitol Records on August 7, 1990, and featured its two lead singles \"Ballad of a Menace\" and \"This Beat Is Funky\". The album peaked at No. 33 on the Billboard Top R&B/Hip-Hop Albums chart."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/18/To_Hell_and_Black.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/To_Hell_and_Black","wikidata":"Q7810959"},{"title":"Hell","blocks":[{"text":"In religion and folklore, Hell is a location or state in the afterlife in which souls are subjected to punishment after death. Religions with a linear divine history sometimes depict hells as eternal, such as in some versions of Christianity and Islam, whereas religions with reincarnation usually depict a hell as an intermediary period between incarnations, as is the case in the Indian religions. Religions typically locate Hell in another dimension or under Earth's surface. Other afterlife destinations include heaven, paradise, purgatory, limbo, and the underworld."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Fra_Angelico_010.jpg/330px-Fra_Angelico_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hell","wikidata":"Q564"},{"title":"Black","blocks":[{"text":"Black is a color that results from the absence or complete absorption of visible light. It is an achromatic color, without chroma, like white and grey. It is often used symbolically or figuratively to represent darkness. Black and white have often been used to describe opposites such as good and evil, the Dark Ages versus the Age of Enlightenment, and night versus day. Since the Middle Ages, black has been the symbolic color of solemnity and authority, and for this reason it is still commonly worn by judges and magistrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png/330px-Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black","wikidata":"Q23445"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/18/To_Hell_and_Black.jpg/250px-To_Hell_and_Black.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/18/To_Hell_and_Black.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/18/To_Hell_and_Black.jpg/250px-To_Hell_and_Black.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATo_Hell_and_Black.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Fra_Angelico_010.jpg/500px-Fra_Angelico_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Fra_Angelico_010.jpg/1280px-Fra_Angelico_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Fra_Angelico_010.jpg/500px-Fra_Angelico_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Last Judgment (detail), c.1431, by Fra Angelico depicting people being tormented in hell","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFra_Angelico_010.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Hel_%281889%29_by_Johannes_Gehrts.jpg/500px-Hel_%281889%29_by_Johannes_Gehrts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Hel_%281889%29_by_Johannes_Gehrts.jpg/500px-Hel_%281889%29_by_Johannes_Gehrts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hel (1889) by Johannes Gehrts, depicts the Old Norse Hel, a goddess-like figure, in the location of the same name, which she oversees","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHel_(1889)_by_Johannes_Gehrts.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Fresque_%C3%A9glise_huaro.JPG/500px-Fresque_%C3%A9glise_huaro.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Fresque_%C3%A9glise_huaro.JPG/1280px-Fresque_%C3%A9glise_huaro.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia